WEBVTT

00:39.000 --> 00:41.836
- It's 4 o'clock! Away with you!
- Change it back!

00:41.836 --> 00:47.050
Jolly Farm Revue. The latest indoctrinating
pablum for children with not enough to do.

00:47.134 --> 00:50.055
Hey! Shut up!

00:55.185 --> 00:59.231
- Wakey wakey, children!
- Good morning, Mother Maggie.

00:59.356 --> 01:02.277
The sun has risen on
another day in Jolly Farm.

01:02.361 --> 01:05.613
Let's see what life's rich pageant
has in store for us.

01:05.697 --> 01:10.285
She has the voice of an angel! And
a balcony you could do Shakespeare from.

01:10.912 --> 01:14.790
Play your song, Melody Sheep,
to aid the little ones' nourishment.

01:14.790 --> 01:18.544
But play softly,
for Pengrove Pig wishes to read aloud

01:18.544 --> 01:22.299
from his magic tome
that holds every book ever written.

01:22.382 --> 01:27.721
"It was difficult for the children of Ipswich
when the lollipop famine cursed them... "

01:27.721 --> 01:32.519
How can you stand watching this?
It's dreck and you know it.

01:32.603 --> 01:36.983
Don't have the guts to respond, huh?
No defence of this unmitigated crap?

01:37.108 --> 01:40.027
Commercial!
I'm getting some graham crackers.

01:43.239 --> 01:47.952
Welcome to KISS Forum, Rhode Island Public
Access's most popular show about KISS.

01:47.952 --> 01:52.625
- Lois, hurry! It's back on!
- Calm down. You know I wouldn't miss this.

01:52.751 --> 01:55.128
OK, let's take a call.
You're on KISS Forum.

01:55.253 --> 01:58.590
- KISS rules! Whoo!
- OK, good call. Good call.

01:58.673 --> 02:01.092
All right. Hey, you're on KISS Forum.

02:01.176 --> 02:04.012
- Yeah. KISS sucks!
- Whoa, whoa!

02:04.012 --> 02:08.266
- Trace the call!
- They suck big time, man. They bite ass!

02:08.392 --> 02:10.479
Wait... I recognise that voice!

02:10.479 --> 02:14.524
Is this Dennis De Young,
lead singer from Styx? Come clean, man.

02:14.649 --> 02:17.360
Yeah. Yeah, it's me. It's Dennis.

02:17.444 --> 02:22.659
You jealous douche. How about I play
"Detroit Rock City" and "Come Sail Away"

02:22.784 --> 02:27.581
and let's see how they stack up side by side.
You want that, you high-voiced bastard?!

02:27.664 --> 02:29.458
We'll be right back after this.

02:30.167 --> 02:34.129
Hey, didn't see you come in.
We're getting into shape for our tour.

02:34.254 --> 02:36.842
We're playing five big shows in five days.

02:36.967 --> 02:39.677
- So if you...
- Rock and roll!

02:39.761 --> 02:43.308
Why don't you just
sit in the corner, huh? Go on.

02:43.932 --> 02:46.352
So if you're a KISS fan in the Northeast,

02:46.435 --> 02:50.106
come out for all five shows
of what we're calling KISS-Stock!

02:50.189 --> 02:56.030
Hell, the Northeast! At times like this I curse
the fact that we live in French Polynesia.

02:56.155 --> 03:01.786
- No, Peter, we're in the Northeast.
- Yeah? And KISS is coming to the Northeast.

03:01.870 --> 03:05.123
That means... uh...

03:05.123 --> 03:08.671
- That means...
- No, no, Lois. Don't help me.

03:08.753 --> 03:11.254
It means we can do something...

03:11.380 --> 03:13.676
Come on, Peter. You're almost there.

03:16.677 --> 03:19.181
We can go to KISS-Stock!

03:25.144 --> 03:26.814
- Yo, Lois!
- What?

03:26.898 --> 03:29.735
I'm packing and can't find
my favourite underwear.

03:29.735 --> 03:31.903
The pair with the rip in the right butt cheek

03:32.028 --> 03:35.573
from stepping on 'em in the airplane
bathroom when you had the trots?

03:35.573 --> 03:39.329
No, with the hole in the left butt cheek
from holding it in for two hours

03:39.413 --> 03:43.584
cos it was a long church sermon and
I thought blowing gas would offend Jesus,

03:43.709 --> 03:47.129
so I let it go in the vestibule
and it sounded like Louis Armstrong.

03:47.254 --> 03:48.798
Oh, bottom drawer.

03:48.923 --> 03:52.468
Tell Mother Maggie what you
want to be when you grow up.

03:52.552 --> 03:53.929
- A scientist.
- A novelist.

03:54.012 --> 03:55.056
A Cambridge don.

03:55.180 --> 03:58.308
What's my future, coming from
these squalid surroundings?

03:58.391 --> 04:00.394
Fighting with a dude at the Laundromat

04:00.478 --> 04:03.940
because he hit on my baby's mama?
I should be there, not here!

04:06.108 --> 04:08.111
London.

04:08.111 --> 04:12.074
Dad, can me and Meg stay up late
every night when you're at KISS-Stock?

04:12.158 --> 04:15.619
Do whatever you want.
Just don't eat from the candy tree.

04:15.702 --> 04:19.165
He's right to caution you. I feed on children.

04:20.209 --> 04:22.586
You don't mind
watching Stewie for a few days?

04:22.710 --> 04:26.256
Nah. Since Jolly Farm Revue
came on, he's been distracted.

04:26.256 --> 04:28.759
- It'll be a breeze.
- Bye, everyone.

04:28.759 --> 04:34.391
My stupid parents are spending five days
following stupid old KISS around. It's painful.

04:34.474 --> 04:37.103
Not as painful as a tyre iron
upside your head.

04:37.185 --> 04:39.480
- What?
- I'll miss you!

04:40.523 --> 04:43.151
Hey, Stewie, what do you want for lunch?

04:43.235 --> 04:46.905
"Dear stupid dog, I've gone to live
with the children on Jolly Farm. "

04:46.988 --> 04:49.282
"Goodbye for ever. Stewie. "

04:49.407 --> 04:53.578
I never got a chance to return
that sweater Lois gave me for Christmas. "

04:53.662 --> 04:57.958
"The receipt's on top of my bureau.
I'm probably over the 30-day return limit,

04:58.043 --> 05:03.257
but I'm sure if you make a fuss,
they'll give you a store credit or something. "

05:03.382 --> 05:05.884
"It's actually not a horrible sweater. "

05:05.968 --> 05:09.639
"It's just I can't imagine when
I would ever wear it. You know?"

05:09.723 --> 05:11.933
"I also left a button on the bureau. "

05:12.016 --> 05:14.102
"I'm not sure what it goes to,

05:14.227 --> 05:17.355
but I can never bring myself
to throw a button away. "

05:17.355 --> 05:22.444
"I know as soon as I do, I'll find
the garment it goes to, and then it'II... "

05:22.570 --> 05:27.784
"Actually, could it have been from
the sweater? Did it have buttons? Hm. "

05:27.784 --> 05:31.831
"I should wrap this up before I start
to ramble. OK, goodbye for ever. "

05:31.955 --> 05:36.836
You know, it might be chilly in London.
I'm going to take the sweater. "

05:36.961 --> 05:38.504
Oh, my God!

05:41.967 --> 05:44.887
One of these planes
must be going to London.

05:44.971 --> 05:46.848
Queue up, children spit-spot.

05:46.972 --> 05:50.310
Here are the tickets, miss. These are all ours.

05:51.144 --> 05:56.651
Spit-spot, Albert Hall, meat and two veg,
Big Ben, Dave Clark Five, pip-pip, cheerio.

06:13.668 --> 06:16.798
- Hot towel?
- Yes, thank you.

06:16.882 --> 06:18.341
Well, come on!

06:18.466 --> 06:21.804
- What the hell are you doing here?
- Taking you off this plane.

06:21.804 --> 06:24.181
Think again, Rover.

06:26.392 --> 06:31.690
Great. I'm stuck on a transatlantic flight
with a petulant runaway. Could it get worse?

06:31.815 --> 06:34.609
You know what I hate
about flying? The peanuts.

06:34.733 --> 06:38.905
First of all, you can't get 'em open.
Who are they trying to keep out of these?

06:38.905 --> 06:44.121
And what's with the razor-blade slot in the
bathroom? Do people really shave in there?

06:44.121 --> 06:49.543
Hi. Andy Dick here. Excuse me. I've got to
get my bag up in the overhead bin here. Oh!

06:49.543 --> 06:51.921
Whoa, no, no! Oh!

06:52.047 --> 06:54.424
Wow, that's wacky!

06:59.763 --> 07:02.557
That wasn't so bad, was it?
Did you sleep at all?

07:02.683 --> 07:06.520
- A little.
- I couldn't. My pillow smelled like farts.

07:06.645 --> 07:09.775
But that's all right because we're in England!

07:09.775 --> 07:11.859
Uh-oh.

07:13.613 --> 07:18.950
But where are its verdant fields, rosy-rumped
maidens and bucktoothed solicitors?

07:19.034 --> 07:22.163
About 3,000 miles that way.
We're in the Middle East.

07:23.123 --> 07:27.586
- Where are we going?
- I'm not familiar with this Arabian village.

07:27.710 --> 07:30.840
Stuff for sale!
Bad, cheaply made stuff for sale!

07:30.923 --> 07:32.799
Hey, Americans. You like movies?

07:32.925 --> 07:37.513
I've got Dude, My Car Is Not Where
I Parked It, But Praise Allah, We Are Not Hurt.

07:37.597 --> 07:40.934
Camels for sale!
This one owned by a little old man

07:41.059 --> 07:45.022
who only drove it to mosque on Sundays.
Just had its knees replaced.

07:45.105 --> 07:49.193
- Buy one and let's get out of here.
- Buy one? All I've got is 50 bucks.

07:49.277 --> 07:51.780
We'll have to distract him. Follow my lead.

07:54.615 --> 07:59.497
"You and I are so awfully different

07:59.622 --> 08:04.211
"Too awfully different to ever be pals

08:04.211 --> 08:06.087
- Do you want to go first?
- Yeah.

08:06.087 --> 08:10.133
"Your favourite hero
is the Marquis de Sade

08:10.258 --> 08:11.510
You're one to talk.

08:11.593 --> 08:14.847
"You get a stiffie from Phylicia Rashad

08:14.930 --> 08:15.764
Oh, one time.

08:15.889 --> 08:20.270
"I've a style flair, just look at my hip hair

08:20.354 --> 08:22.982
- That's quite a nice do there.
- Oh, thanks.

08:23.066 --> 08:24.942
- For me to poop on!
- What?

08:25.068 --> 08:27.445
- You look like Charlie Brown.
- Bite me, Snoopy.

08:27.570 --> 08:33.410
"There's not a whole lot
that we've got to agree on

08:33.494 --> 08:37.373
"Cos I love the strains of a classical score

08:37.456 --> 08:41.836
"And I like that singer
who looks like a whore

08:41.962 --> 08:43.422
- Ricky Martin?
- Love him!

08:43.504 --> 08:47.676
"We're too different to ever be pals!

08:47.801 --> 08:49.971
- " You and I are...
- " Doo doo doo

08:50.096 --> 08:52.681
- " So awfully different...
- " Doo doo doo

08:52.806 --> 08:55.311
- " Too awfully different...
- " Doo doo doo

08:55.394 --> 08:59.357
- " To ever be pals...
- " Doo doo doo doo doo doo dooie doo

08:59.482 --> 09:03.236
"Your head's as massive as a meteorite

09:03.319 --> 09:04.696
Oh, very funny.

09:04.696 --> 09:08.659
"You have a weenie
like a Christmas-tree light

09:08.741 --> 09:13.955
"I'd bet money you'll marry a honey

09:14.080 --> 09:18.252
"Who's pretty and funny,
and her name'll be Ted

09:18.335 --> 09:20.547
- A gay joke.
- I work with what you give me.

09:20.631 --> 09:26.594
"You might think we're in sync,
but we stink as a duo

09:26.678 --> 09:30.433
"Cos you get a kick out of carnage and guts

09:30.558 --> 09:33.686
"And you get a kick out of stroking your...

09:33.686 --> 09:36.065
- You can't say that on TV!
- What? Ego?

09:36.190 --> 09:42.029
"We're too different to ever be pals

09:49.329 --> 09:52.457
Oh, man, we're screwed.
We're lost in the desert.

09:52.457 --> 09:55.669
We have no food, no water.
Our camel is dead from exhaustion.

09:55.794 --> 09:58.924
And I had named him
and given him a back story.

09:59.007 --> 10:03.094
Chucky had the biggest hump of
all the local camels, and was picked on for it.

10:03.178 --> 10:08.100
Then there was a drought, and Chucky went
to the oasis at great risk cos he was like that.

10:08.183 --> 10:12.897
He drank and stored enough water
in his massive hump to slake the thirst of...

10:12.897 --> 10:14.984
Cut the maudlin crap. We're in trouble.

10:15.067 --> 10:19.030
It's below freezing and getting colder.
We're gonna die unless...

10:19.155 --> 10:21.741
- Unless we do something drastic.
- What?

10:21.866 --> 10:25.704
We have to slice open our camel's stomach
and shelter in his entrails.

10:25.828 --> 10:27.914
Eviscerate Chucky?! I won't do it!

10:27.998 --> 10:31.044
- We'll die if we don't.
- All right.

10:33.337 --> 10:36.883
Oh, God! It's like Orson Welles's autopsy!

10:36.967 --> 10:40.011
All right, just hold your breath and go.

10:40.095 --> 10:43.556
- What are you doing?
- Wiping my feet. I don't want to track sand in.

10:43.640 --> 10:47.310
Once you get it in there, you can't get it out.

10:47.394 --> 10:51.483
Oh, God!
I just threw up in his lung!

10:51.483 --> 10:56.572
I know it's gross, but when you're staring
death in the face, you have no choice but to...

10:56.698 --> 10:58.365
Oh. There's a Comfort Inn.

10:58.448 --> 11:00.535
- Really?
- Yeah. Good luck for us, huh?

11:00.660 --> 11:04.079
Actually, once you feng-shui the organs,
it's kind of cosy.

11:09.419 --> 11:12.424
- Isn't this exciting?
- Hey, anyone got a light?

11:13.382 --> 11:14.425
Thanks.

11:14.508 --> 11:18.596
- Look. There's Dave and Dottie, the nudists.
- Hey there, Griffins!

11:18.679 --> 11:23.061
- Dave, Dottie, what a pleasant surprise!
- You're KISS freaks, too?

11:23.186 --> 11:25.897
KISS Army soldier since 1977.
How about you?

11:25.897 --> 11:29.650
'76. I don't think anyone
knows more about KISS than I do.

11:30.485 --> 11:32.779
- What was that?
- It's not important.

11:32.862 --> 11:37.159
- Let him answer.
- No one knows more about KISS than I do.

11:37.159 --> 11:40.996
- Keep it civil.
- I'm not sure I like the tone of your voice.

11:41.122 --> 11:44.668
- Well, throw down.
- Name Gene's special-effects mentor.

11:44.668 --> 11:47.588
Amaze-O the magician.
What school did Paul go to?

11:47.672 --> 11:50.090
New York High School of Music.
Their band before KISS?

11:50.173 --> 11:53.219
Wicked Lester. What year were KISS on
The Jim Nabors Halloween Special?

11:53.302 --> 11:55.721
Trick question. It was Paul Lynde. 1975.

11:55.805 --> 11:59.058
Recite the ad that brought Peter
to Paul and Gene's attention.

11:59.143 --> 12:02.813
"Drummer willing to do anything to make it. "
Rolling Stone, October, 1972.

12:02.897 --> 12:04.982
- Exemplary!
- Rock and roll!

12:07.819 --> 12:10.322
How in the hell are we gonna get out of here?

12:10.322 --> 12:12.825
- Are you going to finish your red paste?
- No.

12:12.908 --> 12:15.827
- What about your sweet, crusty thing?
- Have it.

12:15.953 --> 12:19.789
No more balloon for you! I am sick
of you tooling around the village in it,

12:19.915 --> 12:24.921
honking at the girls, blasting your 1980s
American rock music that we got last week.

12:25.005 --> 12:26.799
- But, Father!
- Go to your palace!

12:26.883 --> 12:28.968
- You know what I'm thinking?
- Yes.

12:29.093 --> 12:33.765
Just wait until they have to
suffer through Jesus Jones. Pee-yew!

12:33.890 --> 12:37.436
- Not that. The balloon!
- Oh, yes. The balloon. Let's take it.

12:38.895 --> 12:42.441
- I didn't know it really looked like that.
- Neither did I.

12:43.275 --> 12:45.360
Such lovely printing, too.

12:49.742 --> 12:51.827
Oh, Lois, here comes the best part.

12:58.293 --> 13:01.003
"And have a wonderful... time

13:02.340 --> 13:04.967
Is that it? No, no, it's...

13:05.049 --> 13:08.513
"And... something something... all day

13:08.513 --> 13:09.430
Right?

13:09.555 --> 13:13.727
- Oh, man. I've lost all faith in mankind.
- Music is dead to me now.

13:13.727 --> 13:16.729
- Hey, now's our chance!
- Let's do it!

13:28.410 --> 13:30.079
Where the hell are we?

13:32.789 --> 13:35.833
Pope... Pope!

13:35.917 --> 13:40.090
- It's time to get up and put on your hat.
- It's a stupid hat!

13:40.216 --> 13:43.551
- Pope!
- All right, OK. God!

13:45.638 --> 13:48.975
- Pope, the floor is not a hamper.
- Man!

13:49.059 --> 13:52.185
It's time to go on the balcony
and address the people.

13:54.689 --> 13:56.274
Aargh!

14:01.698 --> 14:04.617
We gotta find the American Embassy
to help us get home.

14:04.700 --> 14:07.954
I have no intention of
returning to that disgusting hovel

14:08.037 --> 14:12.125
with that intolerable woman,
that fat slob and that insufferable dog.

14:12.209 --> 14:16.714
Oh, you're right here, aren't you?
I stand by it. My future is with Jolly Farm!

14:16.798 --> 14:19.301
- You really think that, don't you?
- I know it.

14:19.426 --> 14:22.763
We've got three days
until Peter and Lois get back.

14:22.763 --> 14:25.766
- Let's go to Jolly Farm.
- Now you're talking!

14:25.891 --> 14:31.189
You make the pope look like a fool!
God will make you pay. Smite them!

14:35.695 --> 14:37.988
He's cooking something up.

14:44.245 --> 14:46.331
I say! Brian, look. Three rows down.

14:46.414 --> 14:48.625
- What?
- Is that Tom Bosley?

14:48.625 --> 14:51.545
Why would Tom Bosley
be on a train in Switzerland?

14:51.628 --> 14:54.048
I'm almost certain. Tom!

14:54.882 --> 14:56.342
- Did he look?
- I don't know.

14:56.426 --> 14:59.762
If I yell, you have to watch. Tom Bosley!

14:59.887 --> 15:01.765
- No, it's not him.
- Oh.

15:03.726 --> 15:06.437
Besides its beautiful historic architecture,

15:06.562 --> 15:10.316
Munich was ze home of many
great writers, such as Thomas Mann.

15:10.399 --> 15:14.488
You'll find more on Germany's
contribution to ze arts in ze pamphlets.

15:14.488 --> 15:16.781
Yeah, about your pamphlet.

15:16.865 --> 15:21.579
I'm not seeing anything about
German history between 1939 and 1945.

15:21.579 --> 15:24.081
- There's a gap.
- Everyone was on vacation!

15:24.081 --> 15:27.211
On your left is
Munich's first city hall, erected in 15...

15:27.294 --> 15:30.965
What are you talking about?
Germany invaded Poland in 1939.

15:31.049 --> 15:35.220
- We were invited! Punch was served!
- You can't ignore those years.

15:35.344 --> 15:38.974
Thomas Mann fled to America
because of Naziism's hold on Germany.

15:39.099 --> 15:42.729
- No, he left to manage a Dairy Queen.
- That's preposterous.

15:42.854 --> 15:46.609
I vill hear no more insinuations
about Germans! Nothing bad happened!

15:52.948 --> 15:55.242
- Uh, is that a beer hall?
- Oh, yes.

15:55.368 --> 15:57.953
Munich is renowned
for its historic beer halls.

16:01.082 --> 16:05.170
- Why is everybody glaring at us?
- Why, Lois? I'll tell you why.

16:05.253 --> 16:08.090
Your faux pas at the concert
was so upsetting,

16:08.173 --> 16:12.136
I had to call a professor to tell me
what phrase to use to describe it.

16:12.262 --> 16:14.763
- Use "faux pas".
- Thanks, Professor.

16:14.763 --> 16:19.226
You've lived a lie all these years.
You represented yourself as a KISS fan.

16:19.352 --> 16:23.107
- And why? To make me look foolish!
- No, to make you happy.

16:23.191 --> 16:28.404
I wanted to share in all aspects of your life,
but I just was never that big a KISS fan.

16:28.529 --> 16:31.950
I should've guessed when you were
willing to dress as Peter Criss.

16:32.075 --> 16:34.994
No one wants to be Peter Criss,
not even Peter Criss!

16:35.078 --> 16:38.208
I guess I'm just not
as cool as you thought I was.

16:38.333 --> 16:40.918
I guess not.

16:43.422 --> 16:46.050
I'm exhausted. Come on, let's get a coffee.

16:49.679 --> 16:53.850
- The smoke is so acrid.
- A man can hardly breathe in here.

16:53.976 --> 16:57.187
You should get some hash, man.
You can't go wrong.

16:57.312 --> 17:01.066
Not true. Ground meat can go
very wrong for me very quickly,

17:01.149 --> 17:03.361
and everyone will suffer the consequences!

17:03.361 --> 17:05.863
You are out there, man, in the ether.

17:05.863 --> 17:09.909
I'd love to further pursue our palaver,
but I'm not fluent in "freaker"!

17:10.034 --> 17:14.289
So, I'm just gonna turn back over here,
back towards my table.

17:14.415 --> 17:16.583
- Are you hungry?
- I wasn't when I came in.

17:16.708 --> 17:20.046
- But isn't that so funny? I'm getting there.
- Same here.

17:23.592 --> 17:28.180
I think
the only reason we die is...

17:28.180 --> 17:31.100
Dude, I know what
you're gonna say and I am so...

17:31.100 --> 17:33.812
Wait, wait, wait, wait! Shh-shh-shh-shh!

17:33.895 --> 17:36.524
The only reason we die

17:36.524 --> 17:40.903
is because we accept it as an inevitability.

17:42.781 --> 17:48.829
- D'you think I'll ever find the right woman?
- Oh, God! Yes, man! Dude, you're great!

17:51.956 --> 17:54.043
Are you ever gonna forgive me?

17:54.043 --> 17:58.631
Lois, I am obligated to keep loving you
so I will take my rage out on my own body.

17:58.714 --> 18:01.008
Let's go to Denny's.

18:02.385 --> 18:04.888
Oh, man! I don't believe it! KISS is here!

18:06.139 --> 18:09.268
We don't deserve to be
under the same roof. Let's go.

18:09.351 --> 18:13.439
All right. I guess I could fix us
something when we... Chaim?

18:13.523 --> 18:17.276
Lois! Do not address KISS
unless they address you first!

18:17.402 --> 18:20.948
Oh, my God! Chaim Witz? It is you!

18:21.031 --> 18:26.162
- Do you want me to sign the left or right?
- No, no, no. It's Lois. Lois Pewterschmidt.

18:26.244 --> 18:28.456
I knew you before you changed your name.

18:28.540 --> 18:31.376
Lois! I don't believe it! It's been ages!

18:31.459 --> 18:36.465
Guys, this is the girl I told you about. I knew
her before we formed KISS. Loose Lois!

18:36.590 --> 18:38.759
- Cool! Loose Lois!
- The legend!

18:38.884 --> 18:42.013
My Grand Slam
was supposed to be with sausage.

18:42.096 --> 18:45.560
I never realised you
were Gene Simmons, the rock star!

18:45.560 --> 18:48.062
You look great. Anyone nailing you now?

18:48.062 --> 18:51.190
Yes, my husband nails me.
This is him. Peter.

18:51.273 --> 18:55.236
- You... are... gods!
- Yeah, thanks. Right.

18:55.362 --> 18:57.530
We're recording in Boston next month.

18:57.655 --> 19:00.786
- You should come on by.
- Oh, we'd love that, Chaim.

19:00.869 --> 19:04.832
I mean Gene, you big rock star. Bye.

19:04.957 --> 19:10.379
Oh, wow! Such a small world.
He was a nice boy, and he's still nice.

19:10.462 --> 19:15.175
Listen, Lois, what I said before...
I've never been more wrong in my life.

19:15.259 --> 19:17.471
You are the coolest girl in the world!

19:17.553 --> 19:20.389
- My wife did KISS!
- And J Geils.

19:20.473 --> 19:21.642
- What?
- Nothing.

19:21.642 --> 19:25.605
There it is! The BBC!

19:28.523 --> 19:31.027
This is it. I'll say goodbye to you now.

19:31.111 --> 19:34.447
- Well, have a good life, Stewie.
- Oh, I shall!

19:35.074 --> 19:38.827
Hey, did you ever find out
what that button on my bureau was from?

19:38.953 --> 19:43.207
- Yeah. Chris's denim jacket.
- Ah. I like that jacket. It looks good on him.

19:43.333 --> 19:45.418
- OK, we'll keep in touch?
- Sure.

19:45.418 --> 19:48.213
Well, I have your address. See ya!

19:50.424 --> 19:52.927
Oh! There's Happy Hill!

19:53.970 --> 19:55.930
What the deuce...?

19:57.098 --> 20:01.687
Pengrove! Pengrove Pig!
Pengrove, I've come to live on Jolly Farm!

20:01.770 --> 20:04.065
Oh, my! The magic tome!

20:04.190 --> 20:09.070
It's cardboard! There are no words, there
are just... What is it you've drawn here?

20:09.195 --> 20:13.992
It's Oswald Owl slammin'
Mother Maggie in a Chinese basket, eh?

20:13.992 --> 20:16.078
Dead brill, eh?

20:17.747 --> 20:22.627
- Mother Maggie, something's terribly wrong!
- Whose stinky brat is this?

20:22.752 --> 20:26.506
That's not your voice! Your voice
is lyrical, like the strum of a lute!

20:26.589 --> 20:29.009
Piss off, ya grotty little wanker!

20:29.927 --> 20:35.057
- It's a fake! It's not real!
- I thought you should find out on your own.

20:35.057 --> 20:37.978
I feel like such a fool. Don't even look at me!

20:37.978 --> 20:43.484
Hey, come on. You wanna get some
ice cream? That'd make you feel better, right?

20:43.609 --> 20:46.613
You wanna get some McDonald's?

20:46.738 --> 20:49.949
You wanna take a dump
in Mother Maggie's shoes?

20:50.074 --> 20:53.620
OK, let's go take a dump
in Mother Maggie's shoes.

20:56.958 --> 21:02.465
- Jolly Farm, Stewie. Don't you wanna watch?
- The Stewie who loved Jolly Farm is dead.

21:02.589 --> 21:05.090
Meet the Stewie who loves funky fruit hats!

21:08.303 --> 21:10.723
Oh, turn it up! Mom and Dad are on!

21:10.807 --> 21:15.812
We're back with KISS Forum. I'm with the
Griffins, and they got something to share.

21:15.937 --> 21:18.857
- Yeah. My wife here did KISS.
- Get outta here!

21:18.857 --> 21:22.403
- Hand to God.
- Peter! How does that make you feel?

21:22.486 --> 21:25.823
I feel like I've done KISS, too.
And it feels good.

21:25.948 --> 21:29.285
Lois, you got any tips for
the young girls in the audience?

21:29.285 --> 21:31.578
The best advice I can give is,

21:31.662 --> 21:35.833
you never know who's gonna grow up
to be famous, so make yourself available.

21:35.959 --> 21:42.216
Cool. Well, that's our show for tonight.
Stay tuned for Battlestar Galactica Forum.

21:42.300 --> 21:44.595
Welcome to Battlestar Galactica Forum.

21:44.596 --> 21:45.596
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru